   <media:title>Kelvin Wave VS Hotel</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/R5KLwDDDzzE?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i3.ytimg.com/vi/R5KLwDDDzzE/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>The Surf and Sand Hotel has been getting hit hard by all the swell we have had this summer.  This part of Laguna Beach is basically inaccessible during high tide these days.  The Kelvin Wave has layered on and additional 18inches of water along most of the Southern California coastline.  This means that a normal 5.5ft high tide is now around a 7ft high tide.  Waves are breaking right on the shore because of the additional water, and in many places there is no sand to protect the structures.  This current ocean conditions have messed up a lot of the local surf breaks but have created some new ones.  Thanks for tuning in to watch us ride out the Kelvin Wave in Laguna Beach</media:description>
