   <media:title>New Water Level Record in Huntington Beach</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/WGjqCNG587s?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i4.ytimg.com/vi/WGjqCNG587s/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>NOAA Tide station observations indicate new water level records along the California coast. This means some of the highest readings in over a century. The Kelvin wave is elevating our seas and contributing to the flooding of low lying areas in southern California. The King tides are finally subsiding towards the second half of the week and the flooding in these areas should calm down.  The extreme water levels this week broke records in many places where they are measured.</media:description>
