  <media:group>
   <media:title>ALL TIME HIGH Sea Levels recorded in Newport Beach: Kelvin Wave and King Tides flood Homes</media:title>
   <media:content url="https://www.youtube.com/v/LiDwiwmJebk?version=3" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" width="640" height="390"/>
   <media:thumbnail url="https://i1.ytimg.com/vi/LiDwiwmJebk/hqdefault.jpg" width="480" height="360"/>
   <media:description>Record breaking Sea Levels were recorded in parts of Southern California today due to a Kelvin Wave paired with King Tides.  The Super El niño has resulted in higher than average sea levels across southern California.  Flooding events like this are becoming more common this year because of the added 12 to 18 inches of sea level thanks to the Kelvin wave.</media:description>
